WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.030
Watch the cloth before you read anything.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:09.410
This roll is a tanmono, a bolt. In the old reckoning, one bolt is one kimono.

3
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:21.090
Its width is settled before any tailor begins. In sixteen thirty-six the shogunate went further, and fixed by law how long and how wide a bolt of silk had to be.

4
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:26.530
Keep that width in mind. Every measurement that follows is counted from it.

5
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:35.370
Now the cut. There is no paper pattern, and no outline of a body drawn on the cloth. The tailor only divides.

6
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:42.870
Straight cuts, across and along, give eight pieces. Every strip has a place, and nothing is thrown away.

7
00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:46.230
Then the pieces are joined again, by hand.

8
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:54.630
The stitches are kept small, and out of sight on the face. Follow the seams: they run straight, because every piece is straight.

9
00:00:54.850 --> 00:01:01.270
There is no dart, and no curve. Hung on its rack, the robe is as flat as the bolt it came from.

10
00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:06.750
And yet it has to close around a person. Come round to the front, and see how.
